# Belt, not braces.
#
# The braces are in `.github/workflows/release.yml`: the build context handed to
# `docker build` is a directory the workflow creates and copies exactly one file
# into, so nothing in this repository is in that context to begin with. This file
# is for the other case — somebody running `docker build -f server/Dockerfile .`
# by hand from the repository root, which would hand the daemon every untracked
# file in the working tree.
#
# The shapes below are `.gitignore`'s, and they are here for the same reason
# (`docs/RISKS.md` R3 and R4): a recording, a consent record or a replay signing
# key that reaches a published image has left this machine, and a published image
# is as irreversible as git history — it is in every pull of that tag.
*
!moba-server

# Named again under the catch-all, so that a future edit relaxing the `*` above
# does not silently readmit them.
corpus/
*.replay
*.consent
*.identity
*.withdrawn
*.session
*.session-part
*.telemetry
*.telemetry-part
*.signing-key
.env
.git
target
